If you mean a **YouTube-style homepage**, here’s a simple HTML/CSS version:

```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>YouTube Clone</title>
  <style>
    body { margin:0; font-family:Arial; background:#f9f9f9; }
    header { height:60px; background:white; display:flex;
             align-items:center; padding:0 20px; gap:30px;
             border-bottom:1px solid #ddd; }
    .logo { color:red; font-size:24px; font-weight:bold; }
    input { width:450px; padding:12px; border:1px solid #ccc; border-radius:20px; }
    .container { display:flex; }
    aside { width:200px; padding:20px; background:white; min-height:100vh; }
    aside div { padding:15px 5px; }
    main { padding:25px; flex:1; }
    .videos { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:20px; }
    .video { background:white; border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; }
    .thumbnail { width:100%; height:180px; background:#ddd; }
    .video h3 { margin:12px; font-size:16px; }
    .video p { margin:12px; color:#666; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="logo">YouTube</div>
  <input type="text" placeholder="Search">
  <div>🔔</div>
  <div>👤</div>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <aside>
    <div>🏠 Home</div>
    <div>🔥 Trending</div>
    <div>📺 Subscriptions</div>
    <div>📚 Library</div>
    <div>🕘 History</div>
  </aside>

  <main>
    <h2>Recommended</h2>

    <div class="videos">
      <div class="video">
        <div class="thumbnail"></div>
        <h3>My First YouTube Video</h3>
        <p>Channel Name • 1M views</p>
      </div>

      <div class="video">
        <div class="thumbnail"></div>
        <h3>Learn HTML in 10 Minutes</h3>
        <p>Web Developer • 500K views</p>
      </div>

      <div class="video">
        <div class="thumbnail"></div>
        <h3>Amazing Technology</h3>
        <p>Tech Channel • 2M views</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```
